    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T15:39:46Z",
    "body": "Issue sweep: partly done on `upstream/main` (`83e5e8a37`). This issue stays open.\n\nDone on `upstream/main`:\n- PR #2904 (`bac4a96c7`) pins `testdata/models/twisted_flank.step` in `crates/kernel/tests/step_twisted_flank.rs`, `crates/geometry/tests/step_twisted_flank.rs`, and `crates/app/tests/import_step_twisted_flank.rs`.\n- PR #2904 (`bac4a96c7`) and `9c5f58e36` (#3767) pin the refusal of `testdata/models/twisted_flank_off.step` in the same three test files.\n\nStill open:\n- The third \"Done when\" item is not complete. That item requires that import speed does not drop by a large factor on the current fixtures.\n- PR #2934 (`543204319`, #2844) left this speed item open (`RECOMMENDED.md` records this decision). `solidcore-tess` still runs its isotropic plan and half-chord replan before `crates/kernel/src/mesh_redivide.rs` replaces runaway strip faces.\n- The issue also waits for the reporter's original STEP file (`waiting-for-user`).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
